public/
.hugo_build.lock
.DS_Store
resources/_gen/
_archive/

# Licensed source maps (e.g. LDS Bible Maps used by permission) — do NOT commit/publish raw
_source-maps/
*.backup-*

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache (contains account creds)
.wrangler/

# Claude Code worktrees & session checkpoints — never track these.
# They had been committed as stray gitlinks (submodule refs) with no
# .gitmodules entry, which made every `git clone --recurse-submodules`
# fail — that is what broke Cloudflare Pages builds at the clone step.
.claude/worktrees/
.session-checkpoints/

# Python bytecode — never tracked
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Contractor and business material — NEVER in this repo.
#
# cfm-corner-site is PUBLIC, and shares one .git with the cfm-week34 worktree,
# so anything committed here is world-readable immediately. On 2026-08-14 three
# contractor documents — including a signed-form animation agreement — sat
# untracked and UNIGNORED in the working tree, one `git add -A` away from being
# published. Nothing had been committed; this closes the gap rather than fixing
# a leak. Business documents belong in the private vault, not beside a Hugo site.
Learning-Inspired-Contractor-Docs/
*-Contractor-Agreement*.md
*-Contractor-Intake*.md
